    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d640">

                <pb facs="0695" n="687" xml:id="pg687"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.981/78a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >krik</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-11-03T21:00:00-05:00">November 3, 1939—9
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>827. For Landreth Harrison. While in Warsaw please discuss with Haering present
                    and possible future working conditions of Consulate General and probable needs
                    of office with regard supplies, personnel, etc. Also discuss political and
                    economic conditions in Warsaw and German occupied Poland. Upon arrival Bucharest
                    submit brief telegraphic report covering discussions and embodying your own
                    observations while in Poland which may be of interest to the Department.<anchor
                        n="31" xml:id="d640-f1"/> A detailed report should be furnished by
                    despatch.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d640-f1" n="31" xml:id="d640-f1-content">
                <p>The economic report, made in telegram No. 2250, December 6, 2 p.m., from the
                    Chargé in Germany, is not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
